{ "Identifier":       {"ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "OSD-IDR-V1.5-I01", "AIMName": "OSD-IDR-V1.5"},

  "APIProfile":       "Basic",
  "Description":      "Identity Reconciliation: reconciles the Face ID and the Speaker ID into a single User ID, and states whether the reconciliation identified anybody at all. The two outputs answer two different questions and are deliberately separate. Identification says whether the presented face and speech match a subject held in Shared Storage; User ID says which subject. A User Agent controlling access reads the first, one greeting a known person reads the second, and neither is inferred from the absence of the other: an output Port that produced nothing can mean many things - not recognised, not run, an input missing - whereas a verdict means one.",

